course: dictionary
lesson: 15758
title: Small and unimportant words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A triviality is something small that does not really matter. You can use it for a tiny detail, or to say that something is not serious. When you meet this word, ask yourself: is the thing being talked about big or small?
explain: Grown-ups often say, «Let's not argue over trivialities.» The word argue tells you people are disagreeing, and the sentence says the thing they argue about is not important. Read the words around the hard word and the meaning often appears.
explain: Notice the ending -ity. It turns the word trivial, which means not important, into a noun, a name for a thing. Trivialities is the plural, so it means more than one small, unimportant thing.
fact: A triviality is something small and unimportant.
fact: Triviality can also mean being unimportant or not serious.
fact: «Let's not argue over trivialities.» means let's not fight about small things that don't matter.
fact: Trivialities is the plural: more than one small, unimportant thing.
fact: Trivia is a related word, but it means small facts, like the ones used in quizzes.
exercise: «She was upset about a triviality, a tiny scratch on her pencil.» What is a triviality here? | A loud noise | *A small thing that does not matter much | A large and serious problem | A kind of pencil
exercise: «The meeting was full of trivialities, so nothing important got decided.» What does trivialities mean? | Brand-new computers | *Small, unimportant matters | Long speeches about the sea | Important decisions
exercise: Dad says, «Don't waste time on trivialities.» What does he mean? | Don't bother to eat lunch | *Don't spend time on small things that don't matter | Spend all day on the most serious jobs | Keep every small thing forever
test: «They laughed about the triviality of the mix-up, then fixed it in a minute.» What does triviality mean here? | *Something small and unimportant | A loud song | A very long journey | A serious accident
test: Sam asks, «Which word means small facts, like the ones in a quiz?» Which is right? | Triviality | Tragedy | *Trivia | Tropical
exam: «The fuss over trivialities made the afternoon drag on.» What is the best meaning of trivialities in this sentence? | Old and valuable coins | Important choices that change lives | *Small matters that do not really matter | Happy songs about the afternoon
